    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "My apologies for the confusion. To report a streetlamp issue in Melbourne, you can visit the City of Melbourne's website and use their online reporting system. Here's the direct link to the reporting portal: [City of Melbourne's Streetlight Reporting Portal](https://www.melbourne.vic.gov.au/streets/streetlights/report)\n\nWhen filing a work order, you'll need to provide the following information:\n1. Your contact details (name, phone number, and email address)\n2. The exact location of the streetlamp (address, street name, and intersection)\n3. A description of the problem (e.g., flickering, not working, etc.)\n4. The date and time when the issue was first noticed\n5. Any additional details that might help the repair team (e.g., if the lamp is part of a series of lamps that are flickering)\n\nAfter submitting the form, you'll receive a confirmation, and the City of Melbourne will assign a work order number to your report. You can use this number to track the progress of the repair through the same portal.\n\nI hope this information is more helpful to you. If you have any further questions, feel free to ask.",
